[{:db/id "q-352710/field-1/6db55cb65769e2a93cdd4d1618397a54c6dcd13bb61f58debeafa28f660122bd" :answer/id #uuid "725a1e6d-47f2-591f-a1d4-0fdfa73436cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352710/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "03b7ca03-3a6f-5d0f-a565-22dff9496f00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352710/field-1/6db55cb65769e2a93cdd4d1618397a54c6dcd13bb61f58debeafa28f660122bd" :answer-field/choices ["q-352710/field-1/6db55cb65769e2a93cdd4d1618397a54c6dcd13bb61f58debeafa28f660122bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352710" :question/id #uuid "0f78ff59-5789-5a85-b29b-9ba1744ba746" :question/math-academy-id "q-352710" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(3-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(3\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352710/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352710"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352703/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "3536d0c9-2cd1-55d1-95a6-99ac566cb0a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352703/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "8c2a22dc-5e93-5f5d-9a4d-fa44b7690e0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352703/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e96ccd4-4541-565e-85b3-4147893ca475" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352703/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-352703/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-352703/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352703" :question/id #uuid "32a9afd7-859a-511b-bf87-a12de0a7f39d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352703" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x. \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352703/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352703"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352491/field-1/3e115fb70cee42c01402b9e71a80760dc16ff9ca054ad4f10305fb512389aa1e" :answer/id #uuid "9dbc422b-c95e-5210-9514-f0c108da69f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352491/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3f8d579-edd7-5e49-885b-d4ff60134b59" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352491/field-1/3e115fb70cee42c01402b9e71a80760dc16ff9ca054ad4f10305fb512389aa1e" :answer-field/choices ["q-352491/field-1/3e115fb70cee42c01402b9e71a80760dc16ff9ca054ad4f10305fb512389aa1e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352491" :question/id #uuid "54568444-95db-52ba-8c35-3ae373af7291" :question/math-academy-id "q-352491" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}8\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity  $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}8\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=5x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=5x.$\n\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{\\pi }{15}$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}8{\\int }_{-\\pi /15}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡5x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{0}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡u-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u){|}_{-\\pi /3}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡0-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)-\\frac{8}{5}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}(1-0)-\\frac{8}{5}(2+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352491/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352491"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114304/selection/470309187a6d89b94d506f0e75bf7421f64f49fd0407355240ab3bc5735acb8d" :answer/id #uuid "f2cee3e9-f14d-5657-a811-73aba5a90c38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114304/selection/e922075c91d70e81f0c78d62c5fef058ca5dcf1e5e2dc6a82fb5d610516012b2" :answer/id #uuid "2ea198b6-6c7a-5099-b6be-a3de0252f133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114304/selection/b4d83d0e488b4236f4ac32228d3229e8d9c61ef4deac512ef95101dcfa8122ef" :answer/id #uuid "299f4206-9551-573b-9992-27f2e505639a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114304/selection/a27d98a46c33c148cbbe546f5c0dbae1bfed5acd32890933d1b4c773adde565b" :answer/id #uuid "b6458493-786c-5814-bbb7-25c682d059ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114304/selection/51fcb3ab094675d4b3402ff8be53e0d9395d3bacc8fd3ad2f3244fe07609c055" :answer/id #uuid "ab8971bf-232f-54d5-a114-5e925701fd1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114304/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc41b769-a9a6-5c26-8a8c-3056228d9575" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114304/selection/470309187a6d89b94d506f0e75bf7421f64f49fd0407355240ab3bc5735acb8d" :answer-field/choices ["q-114304/selection/470309187a6d89b94d506f0e75bf7421f64f49fd0407355240ab3bc5735acb8d" "q-114304/selection/e922075c91d70e81f0c78d62c5fef058ca5dcf1e5e2dc6a82fb5d610516012b2" "q-114304/selection/b4d83d0e488b4236f4ac32228d3229e8d9c61ef4deac512ef95101dcfa8122ef" "q-114304/selection/a27d98a46c33c148cbbe546f5c0dbae1bfed5acd32890933d1b4c773adde565b" "q-114304/selection/51fcb3ab094675d4b3402ff8be53e0d9395d3bacc8fd3ad2f3244fe07609c055"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114304" :question/id #uuid "a6e280b3-86c6-569b-92b8-e8e1faf4b4af" :question/math-academy-id "q-114304" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114304/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114304"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352708/field-1/7a3cd6da119ff65841b87d1769433ebb16d11d58b96023344cfc755c1f24da60" :answer/id #uuid "2804b68d-e698-552f-816f-fdcd770d5fc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352708/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d35b9cb-598a-5ccc-a5f3-3ca50a1fb37e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352708/field-1/7a3cd6da119ff65841b87d1769433ebb16d11d58b96023344cfc755c1f24da60" :answer-field/choices ["q-352708/field-1/7a3cd6da119ff65841b87d1769433ebb16d11d58b96023344cfc755c1f24da60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352708" :question/id #uuid "e032aefb-a1fd-52cf-8ac5-6ccab7ccf5d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-352708" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(2-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(2-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(2-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(2\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352708/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7bd68b3-56ae-57e5-81ef-2370c96664c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352708"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352867/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "4392a908-7c5b-5bf1-b2df-5ae8fb1b5bdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352867/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0bf6752-f563-53fd-9484-5e0143eff8bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352867/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-352867/field-1/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352867" :question/id #uuid "2b77ffca-aefd-5ff3-b060-f3661f8d04e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-352867" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡5x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡5x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=5x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=5x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352867/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352867"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49275"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{8{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74281/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" :answer/id #uuid "bb96d7b3-9717-5d99-ab50-8adf555fbf90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74281/selection/ab3034954fd3e4244af4bd24c1730574690be4960296a549ee68964a5dc5f6d0" :answer/id #uuid "e994a5ae-7c56-5018-af19-5d2d1e6ce644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{csc}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74281/selection/80b0e22de30714fc1acb5ee03d8b0ddebaafbb1768fc2baa39db2b8e234ceb52" :answer/id #uuid "6bb6eccf-cb26-5d94-b0f4-f229b0b43001" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74281/selection/2a39994f286602d32e1a3768fe18ebf50080938f2ec96c670f48997d5130033d" :answer/id #uuid "6b949c26-6189-5565-9235-fdf1db022143" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74281/selection/e770a4aa05c55068674d767662fdf6b662a62daf9ce74ce82c427a4b03d65da9" :answer/id #uuid "caacdc24-510a-5ef5-9877-24e6fe5daaea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74281/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0171627e-b5dd-5d78-a737-dcebdd0dd829" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74281/selection/e770a4aa05c55068674d767662fdf6b662a62daf9ce74ce82c427a4b03d65da9" :answer-field/choices ["q-74281/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" "q-74281/selection/ab3034954fd3e4244af4bd24c1730574690be4960296a549ee68964a5dc5f6d0" "q-74281/selection/80b0e22de30714fc1acb5ee03d8b0ddebaafbb1768fc2baa39db2b8e234ceb52" "q-74281/selection/2a39994f286602d32e1a3768fe18ebf50080938f2ec96c670f48997d5130033d" "q-74281/selection/e770a4aa05c55068674d767662fdf6b662a62daf9ce74ce82c427a4b03d65da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74281" :question/id #uuid "257f803c-0cee-53ae-8960-41eb7bbd6cf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74281" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int (1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int (\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n-\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74281/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74281"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352848/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "b124a922-0289-5551-a1ae-6b3e1d9084fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352848/field-1/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "393336cf-4f22-5f30-b4ee-d26f46b518ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352848/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2598504a-330a-578b-8920-4ee8feb13c9d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352848/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer-field/choices ["q-352848/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" "q-352848/field-1/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352848" :question/id #uuid "bdcc8818-7f26-5426-bbb4-166a2fb17c35" :question/math-academy-id "q-352848" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$  and  $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(1-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352848/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352848"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49284/selection/f34a5f672b366f286527f8e4eebea71975e316697c21aab6851d3123c39791a4" :answer/id #uuid "325c80ea-028f-5699-828a-a7e4841b239d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49284/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" :answer/id #uuid "74e1c9b8-06a6-5c8f-b379-9349a4aba2a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49284/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "6abe06c9-3e5c-5de5-9817-a69add31a5d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49284/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "a31437c6-cacd-5ac8-b158-943a0aeafccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49284/selection/6db55cb65769e2a93cdd4d1618397a54c6dcd13bb61f58debeafa28f660122bd" :answer/id #uuid "03fc3cbd-ebc8-50be-b9a0-3a216ffc4494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49284/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "feb66c0a-62d9-56e2-8b18-3ebd94ca5839" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49284/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" :answer-field/choices ["q-49284/selection/f34a5f672b366f286527f8e4eebea71975e316697c21aab6851d3123c39791a4" "q-49284/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" "q-49284/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-49284/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-49284/selection/6db55cb65769e2a93cdd4d1618397a54c6dcd13bb61f58debeafa28f660122bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49284" :question/id #uuid "96f4b2d2-2c72-5038-ae90-836b7a4eac3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49284" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49284/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347941/field-1/fb98293c21e22d1d5a2328d4987478ba251b016bec263e58e8f7351d2a7680a7" :answer/id #uuid "671e037a-efd0-5cf6-8722-787ae3057537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347941/field-1/bff5e154eea8d1f06c380301d987bf62f60c9d173f996431ab8f2caa6d504dc9" :answer/id #uuid "00d2dddc-f9cf-55a0-b553-b2f196b7eaae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347941/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c9be182-5976-5eb0-9dec-4b6aa38d35d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347941/field-1/fb98293c21e22d1d5a2328d4987478ba251b016bec263e58e8f7351d2a7680a7" :answer-field/choices ["q-347941/field-1/fb98293c21e22d1d5a2328d4987478ba251b016bec263e58e8f7351d2a7680a7" "q-347941/field-1/bff5e154eea8d1f06c380301d987bf62f60c9d173f996431ab8f2caa6d504dc9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347941" :question/id #uuid "7ea22259-6d5c-5d45-907a-d0498167099b" :question/math-academy-id "q-347941" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{9}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347941/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347941"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352798/field-1/b363c90fd31a2d478be07972cfe69c6595ab8d610cad6c742f1db95601907f42" :answer/id #uuid "60f8ff7c-1970-571b-aa1d-3dac08cd6ce2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln(3)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352798/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc76e509-dd11-5428-859f-d33b6556c6cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352798/field-1/b363c90fd31a2d478be07972cfe69c6595ab8d610cad6c742f1db95601907f42" :answer-field/choices ["q-352798/field-1/b363c90fd31a2d478be07972cfe69c6595ab8d610cad6c742f1db95601907f42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352798" :question/id #uuid "071889ac-8c56-50bf-985a-40fa62bb01bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-352798" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352798/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352798"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49277/selection/dbb0c5d7bab0114bcec104596f776de3566a9d5677532083a45cfa31a39369bb" :answer/id #uuid "69803d2a-1cca-5cb0-8683-ed3ef595e264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49277/selection/94bd252c0702de04bd8ec8bd15716ecb55696fa8c1d701dfe696444af333a7a3" :answer/id #uuid "be129e69-7e83-5b33-acfe-987cc572cd53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49277/selection/0496ede2cdc3bdf719d5c9612cef2ecb23341c439ea66c40432b0e279c36d947" :answer/id #uuid "78f5bf7d-8883-5464-84cf-115bdfc285d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49277/selection/a73c5ea78df11c7d4c0ffed5f25a76cdafd8dd5cd7b916f26feb40149cb75ef7" :answer/id #uuid "27097e0b-b9b2-54c9-8f6f-4c912dc2c33a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49277/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82" :answer/id #uuid "dbc3e5b4-10c6-5304-9905-2262af6ca34d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49277/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "394c7ee7-f8de-5467-85a5-ddb40d5f0e05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49277/selection/a73c5ea78df11c7d4c0ffed5f25a76cdafd8dd5cd7b916f26feb40149cb75ef7" :answer-field/choices ["q-49277/selection/dbb0c5d7bab0114bcec104596f776de3566a9d5677532083a45cfa31a39369bb" "q-49277/selection/94bd252c0702de04bd8ec8bd15716ecb55696fa8c1d701dfe696444af333a7a3" "q-49277/selection/0496ede2cdc3bdf719d5c9612cef2ecb23341c439ea66c40432b0e279c36d947" "q-49277/selection/a73c5ea78df11c7d4c0ffed5f25a76cdafd8dd5cd7b916f26feb40149cb75ef7" "q-49277/selection/e346be66d875db07ef40b724e7b05259c06556d266a256aacee203ee49394b82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49277" :question/id #uuid "ac31e6c8-5580-56b9-a41d-519b2407c91f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49277" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}+C \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{-1}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49277/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49277"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362157/field-1/d44fa83f843bb931c0b15366ccb7045f22182cdf2f75578a0b832fc9f01f36a7" :answer/id #uuid "8f31b5be-2f2d-57c6-aa7b-d83104d2a5c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362157/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0da7190-1365-5623-a8c6-964aa6e3029b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362157/field-1/d44fa83f843bb931c0b15366ccb7045f22182cdf2f75578a0b832fc9f01f36a7" :answer-field/choices ["q-362157/field-1/d44fa83f843bb931c0b15366ccb7045f22182cdf2f75578a0b832fc9f01f36a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362157" :question/id #uuid "07b891f5-624f-5ac7-88d1-2d20f03b0610" :question/math-academy-id "q-362157" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{1/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{u}{|}_{1}^{1/2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-362157/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362157"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-2622"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-473"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x } = \\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-474"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x =  \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\sin x }{\\cos x}  = \\tan x$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-475"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
